belgian-azerty-windows (0.9.6) noble; urgency=medium

  * Release build of 0.9.5 (automatic ibus skip, entry below) with Caps
    Lock option A: on GNOME (Zorin) the Windows profile leaves Caps Lock
    as on Linux, because a short Caps Lock tap in a GNOME Shell password
    field can leave apps and GNOME disagreeing about Caps Lock until the
    next login (GNOME mutter issue 3441); with the Windows Caps Lock
    option that makes 2 6 7 9 0 % untypeable. CAPS=windows opts in again.
    Mint (Cinnamon, X11) keeps Windows Caps Lock. The "Belgian keyboard"
    window and both man pages say so. "be-azerty-fix check" says
    "Caps Lock as on Linux" in its profile line when that is the choice.
    A Zorin system updated from 0.9.4.1 or earlier keeps its saved
    CAPS=windows; "sudo CAPS=linux be-azerty-fix system" gives the Linux
    Caps Lock (README, "Caps Lock on Zorin").
  * README: final text for this version.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

belgian-azerty-windows (0.9.5) noble; urgency=medium

  * Fast typing: the Terminal and the text editor skip the ibus input method
    automatically (Windows profile), where very fast typing can swap two
    characters. At every login (autostart entry) be-azerty-fix checks that
    the user has no input method set up (no ibus engine in the GNOME or
    Cinnamon keyboard settings or the ibus preferences, no other framework
    such as fcitx); otherwise the automatic part pauses until it is
    removed. Off with the Linux-standard profile.
  * be-azerty-fix ibus-skip auto on|off|default and on|off|list APP...: per
    user; the "Belgian keyboard" window has a "Fast typing" tick box.
    A skipped GTK app gets GTK_IM_MODULE=gtk-im-context-simple (GTK 3 does
    not know the short name "simple"), through a marked copy of its menu
    file in ~/.local/share/applications, or a systemd user drop-in for apps
    that a service starts (gnome-terminal-server). "off --all",
    "be-azerty-fix uninstall" and removing the package take every marked
    file away again.
  * be-azerty-fix check shows the apps that skip ibus.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:00:00 +0000

