belgian-azerty-windows (0.9.3) noble; urgency=medium

  * New "Belgian keyboard" entry in the app menu (be-azerty-settings): one
    window to choose the profile (Windows or Linux standard) and the numpad
    decimal key (period or comma), in Dutch, French, German or English. It
    runs be-azerty-fix through pkexec (polkit action org.belgianazerty.fix).
  * be-azerty-fix: settings may also follow the command
    (be-azerty-fix system PROFILE=linux DECIMAL=comma), and the user who
    started pkexec gets the desktop settings.
  * be-azerty-fix system: without a desktop session (at boot, over ssh)
    the desktop step is skipped instead of failing.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:00:00 +0000

belgian-azerty-windows (0.9.2) noble; urgency=medium

  * be-azerty-fix: PROFILE=windows|linux. The Linux-standard profile keeps
    the Belgian layout with Linux conventions (Caps Lock for letters only,
    keyd switched off so Ctrl+Alt stays Ctrl+Alt); the Windows profile stays
    the default. The profile is saved with the other choices and shown by
    "be-azerty-fix check".

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0000

belgian-azerty-windows (0.9.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * be-azerty-fix system keeps the earlier DECIMAL and CAPS choice when run
    again without them (saved in /var/lib/belgian-azerty-windows/choices);
    before, a rerun switched Belgian (Comma) back to Period.
  * be-azerty-fix: find the session type through logind, so that under sudo
    a Wayland session is no longer treated as X11 (setxkbmap ran against
    Xwayland).
  * postrm: take caps:be_windows out of /etc/default/keyboard when the
    package is removed, and remove the saved choices on purge.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0000

belgian-azerty-windows (0.9.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * First packaged version. The Caps Lock option, written by hand by earlier
    versions of be-azerty-fix.sh into xkb-data's files, is now owned by this
    package: the symbols file is a package file and the evdev rule is kept
    through a dpkg diversion and a file trigger, so it survives xkb-data
    upgrades however they are installed (apt or plain dpkg).
  * be-azerty-fix: new "uninstall" command; Cinnamon defaults for new users
    and reset settings (Mint); reports every failed step.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 03:00:00 +0000
